CHECK mode == "prepare"

PRINT
    - [ ] Git validation
    - [ ] Evidence/verification
    - [ ] Save/publication
DO Set target from this request/prior explicit choice for this PR, including pr [publish] target
    BRANCH. Otherwise NULL; never infer from defaults/existing PR.

IF target == NULL:
    ASK "Which destination branch should this PR target?" AS target

CHECK target is nonempty and explicitly developer-selected.

DO Inspect branch/HEAD/remotes/operation state once; record current_branch, checked_head,
    repository, push_remote, target_remote. Resolve merge/rebase/cherry-pick/revert markers
    through Git for worktrees.

SHELL `git -C {project} status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all --ignore-submodules=none` AS status_result

CHECK Attached HEAD, clean index/tree including untracked/submodules, and no
    merge/rebase/cherry-pick/revert.

SHELL `git -C {project} check-ref-format --branch {current_branch}` AS branch_format

CHECK current_branch follows explicit naming rules/required validators; otherwise
    <type>/<TICKET-ID>-<lowercase-kebab-description>, exact uppercase active ticket, type
    feature/bugfix/hotfix/chore/refactor/perf/test/release, 1–6 lowercase letter/digit
    description words separated by single hyphens. Count description words only; no ix/generated
    validator.

DO Fetch selected target ref from target_remote; record target_ref (TARGET_REF) and
    target_revision. No fallback base/ref; require shared ancestry, not target ancestry.

CHECK current_branch is a task branch distinct from target.

SHELL `git -C {project} merge-base {target_ref} HEAD` AS merge_base_result

SET merge_base = trim(stdout of merge_base_result)

CHECK merge_base is not empty

DO Set commit_range to target_ref followed by ..HEAD; retain the same TARGET_REF.

SHELL `git -C {project} log --reverse --format='%H%n%B%x00' {commit_range}` AS commits_result

DO Retain all SHAs/full messages from commits_result as checked_messages, including merges; no
    author/ticket filtering or inherited-target checks. Preserve whitespace; only record
    separators/one terminal LF are not bodies. No other trimming, reconstruction, or per-commit
    rereads.

CHECK The PR commit range is nonempty.

CHECK Every message follows explicit naming rules/required validators; otherwise one line
    <TICKET-ID>: <Capitalized present-tense summary>, exact ticket once, colon plus one space,
    meaningful uppercase-start summary, no bodies/extra prefixes/duplicate tickets.
    Add/Fix/Update/Remove are examples, not a closed list. Report failing SHAs/rules; no
    ix/generated validator.

DO Retain branch, checked_head, target_revision, merge_base, checked_messages, and gate results.

PRINT
    - [x] Git validation
    - [ ] Evidence/verification
    - [ ] Save/publication
DO Read full ticket.md/pr.md together; retain exact saved_pr.

DO Review full merge-base-to-checked_head diff/code read-only; verify message accuracy. For
    material gaps, name the missing fact, follow exact imports/symbols into direct dependencies,
    and read relevant ranges. Stop once claims are supported; intent/messages are not
    implementation proof. Retain evidence.

DO Read ../../references/be-human.md once and ../../references/technical-summary.md#summary-content for writing; never run
    standalone summary actions.

DO Compose in-memory draft from code evidence, preserving accurate developer
    notes/labels/order and required Description sections. Title: one concise <TICKET-ID>:
    <Capitalized action summary> line unless overridden. Description follows Summary
    content; read ../../assets/pr.md only for missing labels.

DO Run missing project checks for current code/inputs, reusing unchanged observed results; one
    targeted manifest/Makefile lookup if needed. Probe runtime health only on actual failure;
    request host access on first use. Retain all exits; never mask failures with ||
    true/trailing commands.

CHECK Ticket work complete, messages/summary accurate, no material correctness concerns, and
    required checks passed.

PRINT
    - [x] Git validation
    - [x] Evidence/verification
    - [ ] Save/publication
DO Immediately before save/publish, recheck branch/HEAD/TARGET_REF revision/ticket/operation
    state/full index/tree; compare saved_pr on publish. Revalidate only changed dependencies and
    update retained evidence/checked_head.

CHECK Current state matches verified gate/diff/implementation/checks; active ticket matches
    ticket_id, HEAD attached, tree clean, no active operation.

DO Save draft only to pr_path; successful write finishes prepare, without readback/byte
    audit or push/publication.

PRINT
    - [x] Git validation
    - [x] Evidence/verification
    - [x] Save/publication

PRINT with changed path/observed checks, verified PR URL/state or requested explanation,
    blockers/gaps, and partial success; briefly. Keep checklists in chat, preserve pr.md on publish,
    and inspect remote state before uncertain-write retries.
